217	 * Whether the at-most-one-turn-per-node guard should be released.
218	 *
219	 * Two endings hold it. `handed-off` is work actively going on THIS node, possibly
220	 * after the run that held it stopped. `parked` is work going on UNDER this node —
221	 * the run stopped inside a child-starting call, and the aggregation re-invocation
222	 * is what continues it (#208). Every other ending has handed back — to a person,
223	 * or to nobody — and a node nothing is working on must not stay locked.
